        {
          "source_quote": "ὃν ποτε εἰσεκλάπην χρόνον ἐλπίσιν δονούμενος",
          "english_quote": "the time during which I had once been beguiled, tossed about by hopes",
          "issue": "The meaning of εἰσεκλάπην and its construction with χρόνον remain insufficiently established to accept “had once been beguiled.” The temporal-accusative interpretation is possible, but the draft supplies no lexical or syntactic evidence establishing this particular sense of the passive. The uncertainty note is appropriate, but disclosure alone does not validate the proposed rendering of this difficult clause.",
          "suggested_revision": "Obtain lexical attestations for εἰσκλέπτω and a source-based analysis of the passive, the accusative χρόνον, and ποτε before accepting a rendering. Preserve the supplied Greek and the unresolved meaning note. No emendation is proposed, and the image-checked print should not be treated as defective merely because the construction is unfamiliar. The eventual English must undergo fresh review.",
          "severity": "blocking"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "συννοήσας ὡδίποτε τὴν τοῦ βίου φύσιν",
          "english_quote": "after reflecting somehow on the nature of life",
          "issue": "“Somehow” obscures the demonstrative force of ὡδίποτε: the expression points to a manner of reflection, subsequently illustrated by the following clauses, rather than merely leaving unexplained how reflection occurred.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “after reflecting in something like the following way on the nature of life.” This preserves both the demonstrative element and the qualification without changing the supplied Greek. Review the replacement in the complete sentence.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "συνεφοίτων τοῖς φιλοσόφοις",
          "english_quote": "I associated with the philosophers",
          "issue": "“Associated with” conveys contact but weakens the recurrent attendance or visiting expressed by συνεφοίτων. This recurrence belongs to the verb's contextual force, not merely to an inference from the imperfect tense.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use a source-transparent candidate such as “I regularly met with the philosophers,” subject to fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
